# Vercel manual deploy

Git push does not update epsynapse.com. Auto-deploy is off on purpose (Hobby 100 deploys/day). Follow [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).

## Do not reconnect Git

Do not run `vercel git connect`. `vercel.json` has `git.deploymentEnabled: false`. Keep it that way.

## When to deploy

After commit + push, run `npm run deploy:web` if Vercel serves the file. Pages, browser JS/CSS, `runtime-config.json`, `vercel.json`, and logos count.

Skip `server/**`, `ios/`, docs, `deploy/`, `.cursor/`, `ideas.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `models/`, `ml/`, `data/`, and `scripts/`.

## Command

From the repo root, on `main`, after `git push origin main`:

```bash
npm run deploy:web
```

That is `scripts/deploy-web.sh` → `npx vercel deploy --prod --yes --scope jype1`. It loads `~/.config/jype/vercel.env` when `VERCEL_TOKEN` is unset, because the default CLI login on this Mac cannot see team `jype1`. Then hit https://epsynapse.com and confirm it is 200 with the new content.

Do not invent a second host. If the script still cannot see `jype1`, stop and say so.
